Z||000010||lawrence||09-16-2000||06:16 PM||||No, I didn't see that thread.  I'm usually more cautious than this, but I've never had any problems with Fiero people.  For the most part, they will go out of their way to help you.<P>There aren't any good junkyards near me, so I often work with people who do the salvage trip.  As I said, most of these guys do the work and they don't even charge you for the labor required to remove the parts.  I usually "buy them a beer" by giving them a couple extra bucks for their trouble.<P>I'll send him some conventional mail and see if he replies.  Hopefully, he's just had some time constraint issues that have gotten in the way.<P>-L<BR> <A HREF="http://members.nccw.net/webe" TARGET=_blank>http://members.nccw.net/webe</A>  - WebElectric Magazine||||reg||1
